From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Alp Lab AB <contact@alplab.ai>
Date: Sun, 8 Nov 2026 13:13:43 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] drp: re-initialise on resume only when the hardware was
 running

drp_resume_noirq() calls drp_init_device() whenever the shared DRP-AI
hardware is inactive, including when /dev/drp1 was never opened.
open() powers the block up first (drp_drp_cpg_init()); resume does
not, so on a system where nothing has used the DRP since boot the
first register access in R_DRP_DRP_Open() hits a block whose CPG is
off and an asynchronous SError panics the resume.

Remember in drp_suspend_noirq() whether the hardware was running and
stopped, and skip the re-initialisation on resume when it was not;
the next open() then brings the block up the same way it does after
boot.

Upstream-Status: Inappropriate [Renesas BSP driver added by meta-rz-codecs / meta-rz-opencva, not upstream]
---
 drivers/drp/drp-if.c | 17 +++++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 17 insertions(+)

diff --git a/drivers/drp/drp-if.c b/drivers/drp/drp-if.c
index abf0e83..e6cd182 100644
--- a/drivers/drp/drp-if.c
+++ b/drivers/drp/drp-if.c
@@ -2575,6 +2575,14 @@ static int drp_flag_test( unsigned int num )
 }
 #endif
 
+/*
+ * Whether drp_suspend_noirq() found the DRP hardware running and stopped it.
+ * drp_resume_noirq() re-initialises the hardware only in that case: when the
+ * DRP was never opened, its CPG is still off, and the register writes in
+ * drp_init_device() raise an asynchronous SError that panics the resume.
+ */
+static bool drp_hw_active_at_suspend;
+
 static int drp_suspend_noirq(struct device *dev)
 {
     int result = 0;
@@ -2630,11 +2638,13 @@ static int drp_suspend_noirq(struct device *dev)
     }
 
     dev_info(dev, "suspend: The stopping process has been executed.");
+    drp_hw_active_at_suspend = true;
 #ifdef ENABLE_DRP_SUPPORT_SHARED_MEMORY
     }
     else
     {
         dev_info(dev, "suspend: The stopping process was skipped because the DRP was already stopped.");
+        drp_hw_active_at_suspend = false;
     }
 #endif
 
@@ -2710,6 +2720,13 @@ static int drp_resume_noirq(struct device *dev)
         goto end;
     }
 
+    if(!drp_hw_active_at_suspend)
+    {
+        /* Not running before suspend: leave it stopped, the next open() powers it up. */
+        dev_info(dev, "resume: The initialization process was skipped because the DRP was stopped at suspend.");
+        goto end;
+    }
+
     if(-1 == R_DRP_IsDrpaiHwStatusActive(drp_shared_exclusion))
     {
         /* The DRP-AI is initialised only when DRP-AI is stopped. */
